    "title": "Cosmological Computation and Neural Cartography for the Continental Cathedral",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20126398",
    "publication_date": "2026-05-11",
    "description": "<p>&nbsp;This article presents the integrated architecture of the ARKHE -TEMP<br>v6.1.0 framework, focusing on two complementary computational substrates: Substrate 9001 (Cosmological Computation Engine) and Substrate 6065 (Neural Cartography Engine). Substrate 9001 models spacetime as a discrete causal graph of quantum circuits, inspired by Gerard &rsquo;t Hooft&rsquo;s holographic hypothesis [12], in which each<br>quantum operation corresponds to a spacetime event and wavefunction collapse by an<br>observer generates immutable blocks in a TemporalHashChain (thc) functioning<br>as a cosmic ledger.</p>",
